Z||000004||Raydar||05-18-2001||12:28 PM||||I believe the blocks are the same, externally. Trannies are the same. <BR>The ECM is gonna be a lot of fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>You're probably gonna have to fabricate an exhaust system, too. The Lumina exits to the back. The Fiero exits to the front. <BR>Please let us know how it works out.<BR>I have a friend with a 90 Lumina, 3.1. It's got like 200K on it and still runs good. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||05-18-2001||12:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mr.Frosty:<BR><B>Wait a minute.....Didn't someone used to say that the Lumina minivan 3.1 motor and tranny would go right into a fiero?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The 3.1 minivan motor has iron heads like the Fiero and Camaro 3.4. <BR>The passenger car 3.1 has aluminum heads, and all the other "fun" stuff. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
